  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the child in the VR pod",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the child immersed in the VR pod, as the meme uses the child as a representative of 'kids these days' who rely too much on technology. The user's perspective is aligned with the critical judgment expressed in the text, viewing the child's behavior as an example of the phenomenon being criticized. The child's immersion in the futuristic pod visually embodies the 'rely too much on technology' behavior described in the text, creating a direct analogical mapping where the child represents the stereotyped group being criticized. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the judgmental tone of the text ('smh') and the visual framing imply that the user is identifying with the critical observer role, projecting their own disapproval onto the child's experience.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
